## Company Background
Kinect was created by independent gym operators who needed a simpler, lower‑cost way to run 24/7 access without fobs, kiosks, or heavy hardware. After years of running gyms and experimenting with keypad codes and key fobs, the team built a mobile‑first access system integrated directly into gym management software. Early adopters validated the model during 2020–2022, leading to a commercial launch focused on Canadian independent gyms and studios.
Kinect’s differentiator is native access control inside the management platform. Members unlock the facility with their own phone only when on the gym’s Wi‑Fi, enforcing presence at the door and eliminating the cost and friction of key fobs. Owners and staff can unlock remotely from the dashboard, while the platform handles signups, waivers, billing, scheduling, and reporting.
